 =?UTF-8?q?=20px=20before=20upload?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
Attachment sizing:
- Decode web and desktop image attachments before deciding whether they fit; check both bytes and dimensions, including images already below the upload byte cap.
- Limit the longest edge to 2000 pixels while preserving aspect ratio and the existing WebP/JPEG byte-budget compression path; keep files within both limits byte-for-byte unchanged.
- Reuse the decoded bitmap during recompression, close it on pass-through and unsupported compression paths, and retain source-size refusal and unreadable-image errors.

Guidance and coverage:
- Document resizing for new uploads and recommend crops for small text; previously sent attachments remain unchanged.
- Cover oversized dimensions below the byte cap, unchanged compliant images, byte-budget compression, source-size guards and decoding failures.

Integration details:
- Use valid PNG fixtures in upstream desktop snapshot-delivery browser tests so decoding stays exercised without bypassing the compressor.

- Route desktop preview annotation screenshots and images imported from another thread through the composer preparation helper before attachment insertion, enforcing both the 2000 px longest edge and byte limit. Await screenshot preparation and use prepared image metadata; checkpoint rewind attachments remain unchanged.

- Preserve upstream deleted-chip protection after the final asynchronous image preparation for both downloaded and cached context images; a removed reference cannot reappear while decoding.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. Upstream did not touch imageCompression.ts, previewAnnotation.ts or useComposerContextImport.ts between 3fa57b92a2 and 965ddc1d6c; preview annotation screenshots and images imported from another thread still attach without the 2000 px preparation upstream.

Port to 04f6cfca87:
- Upstream 8fc6fd01d7 now decodes each HEIC photo once, resizes it to the 2000 px longest edge before encoding the JPEG, and stubs the decoder inside every HEIC test. The shared createImageBitmap stub this commit added to the HEIC tests is dropped: no HEIC case reaches the byte-limit decode any more. A converted JPEG still above the byte cap goes through compressImageToByteLimit, which reuses its decoded bitmap and does not resize again; upstream's preview preservation (shared HEIC thumbnail, inherited placeholder thumbnail) is unchanged.

Port to 6b7027b1f4:
- Upstream 7d9c365e17 now fingerprints a downloaded image's bytes (readComposerImageBytes) before it reaches the draft, so distinct images with matching metadata both attach. The fingerprint is taken from the prepared file, for downloaded and cached images alike, because preparation can resize or recompress and the draft dedups on the bytes it publishes; upstream's fingerprint of the preview annotation screenshot reads the already prepared capture.

Port to 6b134a7add:
- Upstream 750e492ed6 copies snapshot images into another composer as image context records that carry their snap-shot source; they enter through the same context import, so they already pass through prepareImageForAttachment (2000 px longest edge and byte limit), and the prepared image keeps upstream's source metadata, byte fingerprint and deleted-chip guard. The browser test keeps upstream's snapshot source on the image record and checks it survives preparation for downloaded and cached images.
- New imageCompression case: a HEIC photo whose first converted JPEG is still over the byte cap is re-encoded as large.jpg from a second decode, without a second resize.

Port to 25875c11b2: Applied without conflicts. An image copied from another thread or environment that preparation resizes now gets its snap-shot source scaled to the prepared size through upstream's resizeSnapShotSource, so the accessibility element tree's imageSize and bounds match the attached pixels instead of the original capture; an image preparation leaves unchanged keeps its source as it was. useComposerContextImport.browser.test.tsx: a new case imports a 3000 x 1500 capture and expects its element tree at 2000 x 1000 (it fails without the scaling).

Port to b6ac2449f1: upstream 055b44919e wraps imageCompression.ts's read errors in m(msg()) and imports gt-react beside the header-dimension import this commit removes; the import block keeps gt-react and still drops the header read. Upstream ad77fd88e2 (Enter during image compression sends once it finishes) tracks pending images in preparingComposerImages around the intake and keeps compressImageToByteLimit as the compressor, so the 2000 px resize, the HEIC over-cap re-encode and the resizeSnapShotSource scaling are unchanged on top of it; 733bc8f1d0 changes docs/user/composer.md elsewhere.

Port to 047fb5b162: upstream 227ac64b74 (#40501, downscaled attachments keep Display P3 colours) reads each image's colour space before decoding and draws on a canvas in that space. reencodeWithinBudget keeps upstream's readImageColorSpace ahead of the bitmap this commit decodes once and reuses, and closes that reused bitmap when the colour read fails; fitImageToMaxEdge keeps upstream's colour space for its 2000 px canvas. Upstream's new imageCompression.browser.test.ts colour cases run unchanged on top of the 2000 px resize.

Port to def64e3a54: useComposerContextImport.ts conflicted only in its imports: upstream 87554a7b86 (#40945, editing a queued message keeps its attachment chips resolved) imports QueuedAttachmentContextBinding and matchRestorableQueuedAttachment beside this commit's prepareImageForAttachment and resizeSnapShotSource; both are kept. A pasted record that matches a removed queued attachment is restored with its uploaded attachment, as upstream does; every other imported image still goes through prepareImageForAttachment (2000 px longest edge and byte limit).

imageCompression.browser.test.ts: Display P3 colour is now checked on the fork's over-cap paths too. The downscale table gains a Display P3 PNG that is still over the byte cap after the 2000 px resize and is re-encoded to WebP from the reused decoded bitmap, and each P3-tagged HEIC is also prepared under a cap below its converted JPEG, which re-encodes that JPEG with the same colours.

Port to b8be2287dc: upstream c3aacf1e5b (#42377, pasted images over 2000 px no longer stall on "Preparing" on busy pages) moved canvas work into imageCanvas.ts and decodes, resizes and encodes in imageCompression.worker.ts, but still reads only the header and resizes only PNG and JPEG. Its fitImageToMaxEdge is replaced by fitImageWithinLimits in imageCanvas.ts, which the worker's "fit" task and the main-thread fallback both run: it decodes once, passes an image within both limits through unchanged, resizes a PNG or JPEG over 2000 px and keeps it when it fits the byte cap, and otherwise hands the decoded bitmap back (transferred from the worker) so reencodeWithinBudget reuses it for the WebP/JPEG byte-budget path, which also resizes GIF and WebP. The source-size refusal still comes before any decode, and a failed decode is still "unreadable". Upstream's off-main-thread browser case runs unchanged. useComposerContextImport.browser.test.tsx: the delayed-import cases hide Worker so preparation decodes on the main-thread fallback, where their createImageBitmap stub can hold the decode while a chip is deleted; the deleted-chip guard runs after preparation either way.

